WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.373 --> 00:00:03.323
Unit twenty. Sleep for Teens!

2
00:00:04.289 --> 00:00:07.962
Hello, everyone! I'm Nurse Bopha, your school nurse.

3
00:00:08.012 --> 00:00:11.841
Hi, Nurse Bopha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.892 --> 00:00:15.785
Today we learn about Sleep for Teens. Let's go!

5
00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:19.697
Sleep. Say it with me. Sleep!

6
00:00:23.182 --> 00:00:27.215
Body clock. Say it with me. Body clock!

7
00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:34.063
Screen. Say it with me. Screen!

8
00:00:37.568 --> 00:00:41.152
Caffeine. Say it with me. Caffeine!

9
00:00:44.655 --> 00:00:48.005
Mood. Say it with me. Mood!

10
00:00:51.516 --> 00:00:55.033
Memory. Say it with me. Memory!

11
00:00:58.511 --> 00:01:02.144
Routine. Say it with me. Routine!

12
00:01:05.644 --> 00:01:09.110
Rest. Say it with me. Rest!

13
00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:23.232
Teenagers need plenty of sleep for mood and memory. The body clock shifts later during puberty. Avoiding caffeine and a screen at night supports a healthy routine.

14
00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:24.624
I can do that too!

15
00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:31.226
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:31.276 --> 00:01:32.426
Screen!

17
00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:38.496
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:38.546 --> 00:01:39.696
Routine!

19
00:01:40.698 --> 00:01:45.075
Did you know? Teenagers need about 8–10 hours of sleep a night!

20
00:01:45.125 --> 00:01:47.214
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:48.318 --> 00:01:55.987
Think and answer. What could keep a teenager awake at night?

22
00:01:56.037 --> 00:01:57.187
Great answer!

23
00:01:58.521 --> 00:02:03.259
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:03.309 --> 00:02:05.841
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

